<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.062 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.062 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.4 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due October 9 was 3.062 percent, down from 3.170 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.1 billion of 173-day T-bills due December 30 was 3.401 percent, down from 3.515 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 364-day T-bills due July 9, 1998 was 3.897 percent, down from 4.013 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$850 million of C$5.0 billion bills due July 17. (Details follow)  </p>
